We have compiled qt4-x11 since moving to gcc-4.6 so the gcc-4.4
optimisation bug won't be troubling us anymore.  However the last
compiled version of qt4-x11 (4.7.4-2) was built on the 7th Jan, so it is
possible it was afflicted by a less troublesome optimisation bug that
was in gcc-4.6 (and is now fixed). The lastest version 4.7.4-3 FTBFS
with an error in the installation phase.  I see it is now being built
again (the buildd state at debian-ports seems to have been reset a few
hours ago so the list of packages that had failed to build has been lost
and they are all being rebuilt again!).

So at this stage I don't have any suggestions how to fix or work around
the crashes.

